    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d473-a2">

                <pb facs="0606" n="526" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg526"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Leishman to Mr. Cole.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-07-06"><hi rendition="#italic">July 6,
                        1901</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: I herewith inclose copy of two
                    telegrams which I sent you on the 1st and 4th instant, respectively, to which I
                    have not as yet received any reply.</p>
                <p>I trust the delay is not the fault of an attempt to delay matters. I am
                    investigating through the telegraph bureau, and if necessary will bring the case
                    to the attention of the Porte, as I am determined not to permit your freedom to
                    be interfered with, and certainly have no intention of sitting quietly and
                    allowing any American who is pursuing his peaceful avocation to be molested or
                    interfered with in any way.</p>
                <p>Awaiting your advices, I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. G. A.
                    Leishman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
